                                                        PROJECT REPORT – 4
                                        Automated Banking Website Using Agile Methodology
1. Introduction

The Automated Banking Website is a web-based application designed to provide digital banking services to customers. It enables users to perform banking operations such as account management, balance inquiry, and fund transfers online, reducing dependency on physical bank visits.

This project is developed using the Agile Methodology, which ensures flexibility, continuous improvement, and reliable delivery of banking services.

2. Problem Statement

Traditional banking systems rely on manual processes and in-branch services, which can lead to long waiting times, operational errors, and limited accessibility. Customers require a secure and efficient online banking solution that allows them to manage their finances conveniently. Hence, an automated banking website is needed.

3. Objectives of the Project

To automate core banking operations
To reduce manual paperwork and processing time
To provide secure online banking services
To improve customer convenience
To maintain accurate banking records

4. Scope of the Project

The system supports customer registration, secure login, balance inquiry, fund transfer, and transaction history. Administrators can manage customer accounts, monitor transactions, and ensure system security.

5. Agile Methodology

Agile methodology focuses on iterative development, customer collaboration, and adaptability. The automated banking website is developed in multiple sprints, with each sprint delivering secure and functional banking modules.

Agile Practices Followed

Incremental development
Continuous testing
Regular stakeholder feedback
Adaptive planning

